      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! For WCAG 2.1 color contrast, check that:\n1. Contrast ratios meet at least AAA guidelines for small text, with alternatives for AA when required.\n2. Color is used effectively with other indicators (like icons, labels) for presentations and visual interactions.\n\nFor screen reader compatibility, ensure:\n1. All interactive elements are properly labeled with descriptive ALT text and ARIA roles.\n2. Dynamic content changes are communicated to assistive technology.\n3. Text-based and image-based content provider options.\n4. Website navigation is easy without the mouse and functions predictably.\n\nAlways test with an actual screen reader and aim for universal access.",
